      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-75348\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">8.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/763#619\">Calculating the Times at Which a Particle Is Stationary</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"75348\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>A particle <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"426\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D443 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> moves in the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"427\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>-<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"428\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> plane (relative to a fixed origin <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"429\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D442 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>) with position vector\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"430\" display=\"true\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" display=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D42B TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mrow space=\"4\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c27E8\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"2\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c63\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6F\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c27E9\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-mrow><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 1em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2208\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"block\" unselectable=\"on\"><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">⟨</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Calculate the times at which the particle is stationary. </p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyHard\">H</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 11:47 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 1:26</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-117278",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(1)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{a}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $-{x}^{3}$ and $x.$\n\nThe integrand ${t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t)+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-(-3{x}^{2}){u}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{(-{x}^{3})}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{x}^{3})+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{x}^{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=-{x}^{3}.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(1).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{1}^{3}+{1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡1 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡1 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
