      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-95169\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">13.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/1942#8296\">Calculating the Derivative of a Cartesian Function With Respect to Cylindrical Polar Coordinates</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"95169\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Given that <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"494\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c210E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> find <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"495\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mrow><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D715\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c210E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mrow></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mrow><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D715\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D703 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mrow></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>∂</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>∂</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> where <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"496\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> are Cartesian coordinates and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"497\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D703 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates.</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 11:55 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:01</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-50971",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following series converge?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n!}$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}$\n\nIII. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the flowchart below to determine which tests to use for each series.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14212321/assets/3aa7f0243efeab51d00aa9694dd018245f7ca4664cc1a5fdf4e646aebb61536e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's test each series in turn.\n\n- For the first series, we use the alternating series test. Observe that \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{n!}\n$$\n\nis positive and decreasing for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, by the alternating series test, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n!}\n$$\n\nis also convergent.\n\n- For the second series, we use the limit comparison test. Let \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nWorking out the necessary limit, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{b}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}÷\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\\cdot \\sqrt{n}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2n}{n+2}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2}{(1+\\frac{2}{n})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+0} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $L=2$ is positive and finite. Now, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nis divergent by the $p$-series test. So, the series \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\n$$\n\nis also divergent by the limit comparison test.\n\n- For the final series, we use the $n$th term test for divergence. Let \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}\n$$\n\nThen, we have ${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=\\infty ,$ since the polynomial in the numerator grows faster than the polynomial in the denominator. Therefore, by the $n$th term test, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}\n$$\n\nis divergent.\n\nIn conclusion, only series I converges.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-50971\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">14.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/1172#725\">Identifying Convergent Series Using Multiple Convergence Tests</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"50971\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Which of the following series converge?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"512\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-munderover><mjx-over style=\"padding-bottom: 0.192em; padding-left: 0.368em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-over><mjx-box><mjx-munder><mjx-row><mjx-base><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2211 TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-base></mjx-row><mjx-row><mjx-under style=\"padding-top: 0.167em; padding-left: 0.058em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-under></mjx-row></mjx-munder></mjx-box></mjx-munderover><mjx-mstyle space=\"2\"><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mrow><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mj