    {
      "dom_id": "question-81106",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}}=-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}+\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{10}}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
