      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-331263\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">57.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/2760#21594\">Graphs of Reflected Step Functions</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"331263\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionGraphicFrame\"><img class=\"questionGraphic\" src=\"/graphics/q-331263\"/></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>The graph of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1708\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D453 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is shown above. Which of the following could be <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1709\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D453 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> where <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1710\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D462 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> denotes the unit step function?</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 2:02 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 5:22</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-81083",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that  ${a}_{n}={n}^{2}-5$ for $n\\ge 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\le 0$ for all $n\\ge 1$\n\nII. ${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence\n\nIII. ${a}_{n}$ is a decreasing sequence",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is defined for $n\\ge 1.$ To determine whether ${a}_{n}$ is increasing or decreasing, we can use the following test:\n\n- If a sequence ${a}_{n}$ is *increasing,* then for all $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}\\ge {a}_{n}\\,⟹\\,{a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n- If a sequence ${a}_{n}$ is *decreasing,* then for all $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}\\le {a}_{n}\\,⟹\\,{a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\le 0.\n$$\n\n- If neither of these conditions holds, the sequence is *neither increasing nor decreasing*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the difference ${a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n} & =(n+1)^{2}-5-({n}^{2}-5) \\\\  & =(n+1)^{2}-5-{n}^{2}+5 \\\\  & ={n}^{2}+2n+1-{n}^{2} \\\\  & =2n+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is *positive* for $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTo see this concretely, set ${b}_{n}=2n+1.$ Computing the first few terms of ${b}_{n}$ we get\n\n$$\n3,\\,5,\\,7,\\,9,\\,…\\,.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement III is false. Since ${a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\ge 0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ we can conclude that ${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-81083\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">58.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/1096#7109\">Determining Whether a Quadratic Sequence Is Monotonic</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"81083\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Given that  <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1724\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msup space=\"4\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> for <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1725\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2265\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"