    "source_text": "\t\nLEARN COURSES\n\t\nJP\nMATHEMATICAL METHODS FOR THE PHYSICAL SCIENCES II: PLACEMENT EXAM\nAnalysis\nPrecalculus\nIII. Inequalities\nCorrect 8.1. Solving Radical Inequalities\nCalculus I\nVIII. Integration\nCorrect 24.1. Approximating Areas With the Left Riemann Sum\nCorrect 24.2. Approximating Areas With the Right Riemann Sum\nCorrect 27.2. The Second Fundamental Theorem of Calculus\nCalculus II\nII. Applications of Integration\nCorrect 11.1. Surface Areas of Revolution: Rotation About the X-Axis\nCorrect 11.3. Surface Areas of Revolution for Parametric Curves\nIII. Parametric & Polar Equations\nCorrect 15.1. Calculating Velocity for Plane Motion Using Differentiation\nIncorrect 15.5. Applying Newton's Second Law in the Plane\nCorrect 16.2. Further Differentiation of Curves Given in Polar Form\nIV. Sequences & Series\nCorrect 18.1. Monotonic Sequences\nCorrect 21.5. The Comparison Test\nCorrect 21.13. Selecting Procedures for Analyzing Infinite Series\nCorrect 22.3. Third-Degree Taylor Polynomials\nCorrect 23.3. Maclaurin Series\nMathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II\nI. Projections\nCorrect 1.4. The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers\nIncorrect 2.7. Orthogonal Sets in Inner Product Spaces\nIncorrect 2.9. Orthogonal Linear Transformations\nCorrect 3.2. The Components of a Vector with Respect to an Orthogonal or Orthonormal Basis\nIncorrect 3.7. Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Inner Product Spaces\nCorrect 4.2. The Gram-Schmidt Process in the General Case\nII. Quadratic Forms\nCorrect 6.6. Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms: Determining Where Extrema are Attained\nCorrect 6.6. Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms: Determining Where Extrema are Attained\nCorrect 7.2. Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix\nIII. Applications of Linear Algebra\nCorrect 8.4. Weighted Least-Squares\nIV. Multiple Integrals\nCorrect 9.4. Triple Integrals Over Type I Regions\nIncorrect 9.9. Changing the Order of